      "post_id": "79219",
      "author_handle": "hannahbryden",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 17 years 7 months ago",
      "body": "Hi\nI am just getting ready to have my 1st (3 weeks to go) and I need your advice please.\nI have a cot and have just bought a Graco Travel cot with Bassinett, the only things is I dont know what should go in either of them? what baby should wear etc\nI live in a warm climate in Dubai and have the luxury of Ac or not.\nI am guessing baby will go to sleep in an all in one babygrow suit thingy, but else????Should I have a fitted sheet? WHat will keep him/her warm? They say no blankets?\nI am so confused and worried now please help\nPlease don't give out personal details in the forum",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-8268/#79219",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/8da31b0fcac78bf54bf9.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-8268/",
      "role": "original_post",
      "original_post_id": "79219"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "79235",
      "author_handle": "Samuel",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 17 years 7 months ago",
      "body": "We put them in an all in one then a sleep suit, the kind that are like a sleeping bag with arms, you can get different thicknesses for summer and winter.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-8268/#79235",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/8da31b0fcac78bf54bf9.html",
      "page_url": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-8268/",
      "role": "response",
      "original_post_id": "79219"
    },
    {
      "post_id": "79238",
      "author_handle": "candgsmum",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 17 years 7 months ago",
      "body": "I had my son during a hot summer so he often just went into his mosses basket in his nappy or a vest. If he seemed cold I would put a blanket on him or a light cotton sheet.\nI good way to check they are warm is to put the back of your hand on their neck or back if they feel hot to touch the are too warm, if they feel cold add a layer.\nI had a a nursery monitor which indicated whether the room was hot or cold.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-8268/#79238",
      "raw_file": "_raw/forums-deep/justparents/responses/8da31b0fcac78bf54bf9.html",
